# Database and server APIs

Postgres (Supabase) is the source of truth. Prompt context is assembled
from stored project state, not chat history.

Tables: profiles, projects (jsonb state), papers, orient_checks,
decisions, messages, summaries, proposed_patches. Every table has RLS scoped to
`auth.uid()`.

```sql
-- ✅ GOOD
create policy "own projects" on projects
  for all using (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

- Model (Groq/Gemini) and paper-search (OpenAlex) calls run server-side only.
- Citations must reference rows in `papers` or real OpenAlex results from
  `recommend_readings`. Never persist invented references.
- Model tools `update_state`, `add_paper`, `log_decision` return
  **proposed** patches. Validate with zod before save; apply only after
  user accept. `update_profile` (profile fields only) is applied directly.
- New migrations must be idempotent; see `supabase/migrations/`.
- `lib/prompt/assemble.ts` stays a pure function with unit tests.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
await fetch("https://api.groq.com/...", { headers: { Authorization: key } }) // in a client module

// ✅ GOOD
// src/app/api/chat/route.ts using server-only env keys
```
